WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.500
The fate of the universe lies on your shoulders.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.120
Now, whatever you do...

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.040
...don't... push... this... button.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.600
Because that will set off the bomb immediately           and we'll all be dead.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.260
[scandalised gasp]

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.100
Now, repeat back what I just said.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:24.840
I am Groot.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.840
No! No, that's the button that will kill everyone!

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:29.100
Try again.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:30.220
I am Groot.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.480
I am Groot.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:34.620
I am Groot.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.720
No!

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.780
Showtime, a-holes!

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:00.780
Screw you, space shits!

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.860
Does anybody have any tape out there?
I want to put some tape over the death button.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.500
-Nobody has any tape!
-Not a single person has tape?!

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.300
You have an atomic bomb on your bag!

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.300
If anybody's going to have tape, it's you!

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.780
-I have to do everything!
-You are wasting a lot of time!

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.580
I am Groot!

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:30.780
That's a really bad sign.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.660
If I touch someone, I can feel their feelings.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.320
You feel... love!

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.540
Yeah, I guess I feel a general unselfish love for just about...

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.340
-No! Sexual love!
-No! No, I don't!

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.720
-For her!
-No!

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:00.660
She just told everyone your deepest, darkest secret!

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.640
Dude, come on! I think you're overreacting a little bit.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.500
You must be so embarrased!

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.500
Do me! Do me, do me!

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.980
Hey, Youtubers.
I am Groot, we are Groot.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.220
New guardians footage. Let's break it down.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.520
And there is a new round of the Spider-Man
giveaway going on.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:22.620
So all you do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment on this video.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.660
Be sure to click the bell to turn alerts on
so you don't miss anything.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:33.500
So, giant space tentacle monsters! Marvel Phase 3
is like full Rick and Morty: maximum tentacle.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.000
It's like the Cronenberg universe.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.820
This is basically like the interdimensional being
that James Gunn explained

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:43.560
that the team is hired to take down by Ayesha,
played by Elizabeth Debicki.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:49.880
They have this really weird relationship
where she belongs to this  genetically perfect race
that's super uptight.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:54.560
Things go sideways, then she ends up coming after Peter Quill and the Guardians.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.760
But like this is like one of the big action set pieces here when they go all cray.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.700
You can see Dax just stabbing the crap out of it.
It's just so hilarious.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.900
So, if you couldn't tell from all the baby Groot
that they put in this,

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.300
they're just trying to imply
the tone, the humor...

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.980
and give you an idea for how the upped the scale.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.840
So, there's a whole lot we don't see in here
but we're one step closer to seeing Ego

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:18.800
because we see Mantis, who has been living with Ego her whole life.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:23.480
She's Peter Quill's half-sister by Ego, the living planet.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.860
So, I know that just sounds mind-boggling.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:30.290
So don't worry about that they'll totally
explain how he made himself a human body

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.820
and was able to procreate with the human woman

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.540
but Gunn has just said that, thematically,
the way he works in the film

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.620
is that he's this ancient being
like we learned in the last film.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.980
Peter Quill has ancient DNA in  him.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.940
And he's been so lonely like he's been a living planet.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:49.980
How many other living planets
do you know about in the universe.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:54.040
So, being so lonely,
that's why he made himself a human body

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.040
so that he could make himself a family.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.040
Family is like one of the biggest things about this movie,

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:03.680
finding your biological family,
like, Peter Quill searching for his father;

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.820
the Guardians themselves as a family...
Like the family you make for yourself

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.740
versus the family are born into.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:13.060
So if you want to, you could consider
Ego, the living planet,

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:17.760
the big villain of the film. But in terms of actual villains that you would actually go up against,

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.740
you have the Ravagers, like we saw in the first trailer.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.440
They mutiny against Yondu,
so the Guardians have to help him escape.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.620
That forms the basis for why Yondu
is part of the Guardians.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:33.280
He was part of the original Guardians team in the comics. So now he looks more like original Yondu

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.020
and he's doing more original Yondu things.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.880
But Michael Rooker's going to be crazy in this. So it''ll be a lot of fun.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:43.680
They still haven't said anything about Sylvester Stallone's mystery performance,

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:48.600
but he wears a Ravagers uniform but I think he goes beyond being a normal Ravager.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:53.780
But speaking of which... They put baby Groot
in a tiny-baby Ravagers uniform.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:56.180
You just see him go crazy through most of the trailer.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:00.020
So this is kind of like the trailer that you would show off to like little kids to.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:03.940
I feel like they kept him a little baby
just for the younger audience,

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.420
just because you see so many little kids
going to comic book conventions

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.020
dressed with like baby Groot cosplay.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:14.940
So keeping him a baby for most of the film,
maybe not the entire film but most of the film,

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:16.560
allows them to have a little bit more fun.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.400
Like: "Don't press this little red
button that is going to kill everybody."

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.220
But, if you haven't read the comics,

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:26.660
Groot is effectively immortal.
As long as you have like a little piece of his bio matter.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:31.040
He can completely regrow himself
from even the littlest of twigs

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:36.470
but they said in the movie he won't
have most of original Groot's memories

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:38.790
but he's effectively the same Groot.

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:44.360
You're getting a Groot
with a vastly different personality,
but effectively it's the same character,

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.560
the "We are Groot" type person.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:49.130
So there will probably be a moment in this
like there was in the first film

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:52.080
and I do think we'll see him grow
towards the end of the film,

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:54.740
but for most of it
he's probably going to be dancing baby Groot.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:58.580
But it actually doesn't take him that long
to regrow himself in the comics.

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:01.460
Like he could actually do it
in a relatively short amount of time.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:07.500
A lot of you have also
probably noticed that Nathan Fillion
has a cameo as Wonder Man in the movie,

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:12.460
that they have a slightly different
spin on the character but it is Wonder Man from the comics.

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:16.240
He had a  cameo in the first film
but he was like a full-CG character

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:19.260
So, you really just had to listen to his voice
to know that it was him,

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.500
but this time you actually see his face on camera.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:25.780
But the other big thing they're selling this romance between Star Lord and Gamora.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:26.900
-No, I don't.
-For her!

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:27.540
No!

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:33.260
She just told everyone your deepest, darkest secret!

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:35.500
Dude, come on! I think you're overreacting a little bit.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.240
You must be so embarrased!

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:41.280
Do me! Do me, do me!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:45.240
They kind of had some chemistry in the comics
  but they haven't really been doing that recently.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:48.900
They had adventures with Captain Marvel,
Ironman joined them for a while...

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:52.620
They're kind of mixing and matching them
with other Marvel mainstream characters

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:56.260
but we won't actually see the Guardians
with the other Avengers

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.740
'till Infinity War.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:02.620
And otherwise it looks really good.
Like it obviously took them a long time
 to get these special effects down.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.900
The movie's been done for a while
but they still had to do post-production.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.860
so let me know you guys think.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:11.740
I just I love the way James Gunn uses color,
he has a really good sense of humor,

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:14.440
he has a really clear idea for the story 
he wants to tell

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:17.360
so the narrative usually doesn't get too muddied down,

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:20.740
like it doesn't fall into a lot of the tropes
of big superhero films

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:22.360
that you saw earlier this year

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:25.560
with films that probably got released
before they were ready to be.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.320
One of the most fun things about
James Gunn though... like I mean is a great filmmaker

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:32.900
but is also really vocal, he has
like a really strong connection with the fandom.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:35.760
So he is like a lifelong comic book nerd.

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:38.760
So I just feel like that helps him
make really good comic book movies

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:42.880
because he understands the characters
and he understands the way comic books work.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:46.180
So just a reminder that this is coming out May 2017.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.090
They'll probably do like another big Super Bowl trailer.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:52.010
There'll probably be some Spider-Man: Homecoming before then, too,

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:56.360
Star Wars Episode VIII
will probably be held for celebration...

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:00.020
They might do a Super Bowl trailer
but now the were like approaching the end of the year

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:03.400
everybody is just like blowing it up for 2017.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:08.060
The amount of awesome stuff
that's happening next year is unbelievable.

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:10.480
Even the TV stuff, too. It's just off the charts.

